<title>JAPAN: Japan June raw sugar imports down 8.16 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan June raw sugar imports down 8.16 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's raw sugar imports in June totalled 151,904 tonnes, down by 8.16 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			   June 97     May 97	  June 96</p>
<p> Total		  151,904     140,555	 165,400</p>
<p>Main suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand		56,594	74,931	 104,388</p>
<p> Australia	     23,495	23,882	     nil</p>
<p> Cuba		    71,815	41,742	  61,012</p>
<p>Total imports in the first six months of calendar 1997 reached 738,560 tonnes, against 740,465 tonnes during the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
